A pricing-page shape (`featureCell`/`featureTitleCell`):
`merge(featureCell{padding: 4px $(gap)}, featureTitleCell{padding-top:
0; padding-bottom: 0})` - `featureTitleCell` is meant to override
`featureCell`'s vertical padding. `featureCell`'s block has a SECOND
interpolated declaration too (its own accent color), so its
`padding: 4px $(gap)` is a genuine two-declaration `_in_` bundle - opaque to
`CSS.merge`, which can't see a property inside a bundle to drop it. Real
sheet positions put `featureTitleCell`'s longhand atoms EARLIER (2564,
5488) than `featureCell`'s bundle (7082): same specificity, so without an
order the LATER rule - the bundle's own `padding: 4px 16px` - wins over the
two `0` overrides that were supposed to override it.

The ppx records the merge in `[@@@css.merges]` (each argument as the index
of its block), and generate puts each competing rule of `featureCell`
before each rule of `featureTitleCell`:

  $ cat > pricing.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css ("._a_titlepad1{padding-top:0;}", "_a_titlepad1", "0,1,0 own", "padding", 8, false)]
  > [@@@css ("._a_titlepad2{padding-bottom:0;}", "_a_titlepad2", "0,1,0 own", "padding", 2, false)]
  > [@@@css ("._in_pricingcell{padding:4px 16px;}", "_in_pricingcell", "0,1,0 own", "padding", 15, false)]
  > [@@@css ("._in_pricingcell{color:var(--accent);}", "_in_pricingcell", "0,1,0 own", "color", 1, false)]
  > [@@@css.bindings [("Pricing.featureTitleCell", "_id_title", "_a_titlepad1 _a_titlepad2"); ("Pricing.featureCell", "_id_cell", "_in_pricingcell")]]
  > [@@@css.blocks [(1, "_id_title", [0; 1]); (2, "_id_cell", [2; 3])]]
  > [@@@css.merges [(3, [1; 0])]]
  > EOF

  $ styled-ppx.generate pricing.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._in_pricingcell{padding:4px 16px;}
  ._a_titlepad1{padding-top:0;}
  ._a_titlepad2{padding-bottom:0;}
  ._in_pricingcell{color:var(--accent);}

The two `0` longhands now come after the bundle's `padding` and win on the
top and bottom sides, as the call order of `merge(featureCell,
featureTitleCell)` says. Without the merge, no block lists both bindings'
rules, and definition order keeps the bundle last:

  $ sed '/css.merges/d' pricing.ml > no_merge.ml
  $ styled-ppx.generate no_merge.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._a_titlepad1{padding-top:0;}
  ._a_titlepad2{padding-bottom:0;}
  ._in_pricingcell{padding:4px 16px;}
  ._in_pricingcell{color:var(--accent);}

Generate adds no "shorthand before a longhand it covers" edge: such an
edge also reaches through an unrelated block's longhand and can pull a
merge's later argument ahead of the earlier one (see
`ordered-sheet-monorepo-regressions.t` in the ppx tests).
